      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "CLI dispatcher + lifecycle registration\nHost builds registry, transport, startup, launcher, observer, terminator",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#detail-coupling",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "DaemonProcessCoordinator\nCLI-local process entry and worker entry",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#detail-authority",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "38 frozen compatibility mechanism files\nexecution · delivery · registry · transport · worker · resources · lifetime · diagnostics",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#detail-staging",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "DaemonClient → private Node runtime\nHost calls execute() or control(); no mechanism factories in its public contract",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#detail-coupling",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "Routing + lifecycle composition\nguards · registry · transports · controller · startup",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#detail-routing",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "Package process entry + worker entry\nInjected host executor still supplies product behavior",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#detail-coupling",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "The host knows too much ↗",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#detail-coupling",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D01\nGive hosts execute and typed control reports\nSTATED\n\nHosts supply environment, executor factory + module URL, readiness probe, and classified requests. The client returns output + mode or a lifecycle report.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D01",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D02\nKeep declarations free of Node types\nSTATED\n\nThe façade dynamically loads its Node runtime during construction. Portable declarations do not make execution browser-compatible.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D02",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D03\nPackage the process and worker around injected execution\nSTATED\n\nThe package owns executable entries and private mechanisms; the host executor still supplies product behavior. The daemon imports no other production symnav package.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D03",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "The old route is still connected ↗",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#detail-staging",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D04\nKeep the shipped CLI on its compatibility graph\nSTATED\n\nThe dispatcher and lifecycle registration remain byte-identical to the base. This PR adds the package path; it does not switch those consumers.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D04",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D05\nFreeze 38 app-local mechanism files\nSTATED\n\nA path-and-content hash freezes the compatibility graph after preparation. It normalizes CRLF; dispatcher, route, and workspace selector are excluded.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D05",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D06\nGroup mechanisms by the concern they own\nSTATED\n\nClient, process, registry, transport, execution, delivery, worker, resources, diagnostics, and lifecycle become package folders. The coordinator is renamed before copying.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D06",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "The first answer ends the search ↗",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#detail-routing",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D07\nUse four ordered, lazy routing guards\nSTATED\n\nRecord present → not starting → version → responsive. Read and observation are memoized; a decision prevents every later guard and its effects.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D07",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D08\nKeep the route and local-execution distinctions\nSTATED\n\nDisabled, absent, starting, or recovering run cold; ready/busy run warm; dead/incompatible fall back. Only absent/fallback routing decisions trigger independent warmup. Local attempts get fresh executors. Errors and exact-process cleanup keep their distinct routes.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D08",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D09\nCompose lifecycle once, with a separate status timeout\nSTATED\n\nDisabled blocks start; status and stop still operate. The host supplies the readiness command, which still runs through execution. Control failures reject to the host wrapper.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D09",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "A missing answer is not permission to replay ↗",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#detail-delivery",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D10\nLet transport retry-safety authorize fallback\nSTATED\n\nA retry-safe warm submission failure gets one local fallback. An uncertain or accepted failure stays warm and produces a controlled failure instead of replay.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D10",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D11\nOwn warm output capture inside the package\nSTATED\n\nEach transfer gets a fresh policy-limited capture, using memory then an OS-temporary spool. The returned output still has records() and dispose(); the host does not provide capture factories.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D11",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D12\nOwn failure output and malformed-result cleanup\nSTATED\n\nResource, response-capacity, and incomplete-request failures become stderr + exit 1. A missing output or non-integer exit code is incomplete; any available malformed output is disposed.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D12",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "Who is allowed to act? ↗",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#detail-authority",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D13\nValidate adopted coordinates inside the coordinator\nUNEXPLAINED\n\nThe renamed coordinator takes coordinates, a serving port, a workspace-exists callback, and an explicit clock. Identity mismatches fail before component setup; that placement has no stated rationale.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D13",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D14\nGive registry startup equality one owner\nSTATED\n\nCallers request named identity/instance/token/PID checks. One predicate compares the requested coordinates; exact-owner cleanup also compares timestamps and revision.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D14",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D15\nPin the existing authentication order and exceptions\nUNEXPLAINED\n\nExecution checks protocol/instance before token. Identify/terminate/kill use identity credentials; ping/stop still omit token checks. No reason for that asymmetry was found.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D15",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D16\nUse a daemon-owned clock API\nSTATED\n\nDaemon mechanisms stop using telemetry clocks and raw time sources. Wall time still owns persisted/lifetime deadlines; monotonic time owns elapsed execution and queue measurements.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D16",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D17\nDefer readiness- and completion-based idle timing\nSTATED\n\nIdle time starts in the constructor and resets at navigation acceptance. Long startup or a long completed turn can exhaust it. Ready/completion resets are written down as future behavior.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D17",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "The witnesses changed too ↗",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#detail-witnesses",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D18\nMove 37 mechanism test files into the daemon package\nSTATED\n\nPackage tests use generic executor fixtures and local helpers, including standalone module fixtures and tsx tooling. CLI product behavior stays with CLI tests.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D18",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D19\nNarrow the relocated worker test\nUNEXPLAINED\n\nGeneric readiness replaces the CLI version scenario and drops startup/execution duration assertions. Version rejection returns as a direct CLI-factory test, losing the former worker-initialization assertion.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D19",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D20\nReplace the mocked CLI entry tests with built-entry evidence\nSTATED\n\nThe CLI entry test file is deleted. New package tests exercise compiled worker, launcher, process initialization, and cleanup. They test a different boundary, not the same mock assertions.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D20",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D21\nRetire policy-testing exports and their lint guard\nUNEXPLAINED\n\nThe export map becomes root + two side-effect-only entries. Policy helpers move to test folders; the old import restriction and its positive/negative tests are deleted.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D21",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D22\nAdd a clock-ownership scan limited to one folder\nUNEXPLAINED\n\nThe new test scans only siblings of lifecycle/daemon-clock.test.ts. Process, registry, worker, and execution folders are outside its scope.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D22",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D23\nDisable parallel execution of package test files\nUNEXPLAINED\n\nThe new Vitest configuration sets fileParallelism: false. No explanation accompanies this choice.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D23",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "D24\nGive Windows termination a different cleanup assertion\nUNEXPLAINED\n\nThe built-process test permits a retained record and absent termination diagnostic on Windows, then has its caller remove the exited record. Other platforms expect process cleanup.\n\nreason + evidence ↗",
      "id": "decision-D24",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
